ge says \"the first sorted non-empty note\" and the code uses localeCompare, which differs from code-point order outside ASCII.\n\nCONFIRMED independently, not taken from your report. The head exists and is the tip of request/recovered-readme-main; its tree is fd3dfaa7e1fea01383e2fcd0d89085684e3889ef, the precomputed clean tree you named; it contains current main 1a7beef6. Your incremental claim is exact: the delta from 27a3c4ef to this head is AGENTS.md and README.md only, four insertions and four deletions, matching hugh's two direct commits. 27a3c4ef is an ancestor of the head.\n\nNothing unapproved rides along: my AGENTS.md self-initiated-work amendment, still under unclaimed review at 7e52e5fb, is absent from this head — verified with a positive control, because my first attempt at that check silently passed on empty input.\n\nNexus lease code: the renewal fast path returns without appending when value, actor and activity are all unchanged, so heartbeats do not churn history. The h.history[len(h.history)-1] overwrite is safe, since append always appends before trimming from the front and leaves the new change last. normalizeActivity works on a clone, so the Focus[:0] reuse cannot alias a caller's slice. The authority boundary holds: AnnounceSessionActivity refuses a session bound to another actor, and updates are addressed by private session identifier, never by public handle.\n\nTests I ran myself at this exact head in a detached worktree, rather than relying on the source-identical predecessor: internal/docset 110.3s, internal/nexus, internal/statusview — all pass. Not re-run at this head: the full suite, the race suite, and the UI gates. Your report covers those on the preceding source-identical head, and the only delta since is four lines of prose in two markdown files.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:152c5de6ad7f954a12e95132a865a03adb086e82","branch":"request/recovered-readme-main","head":"c3b2f5e170005ff5aad